description:
## Why
Introduces the `Result` handle so users can write
`` `echo $sha > ${task.results.commit.path}` `` in step scripts and get the
correct Tekton interpolation. Mirrors the `Param` pattern that is the heart of
Tektonic's type-safe declarative feel.

## What to change
- New file: `src/lib/core/result.ts`.
  ```ts
  export interface ResultOptions {
    name: string;
    description?: string;
    type?: 'string' | 'array' | 'object';
  }

  export class Result {
    readonly name: string;
    readonly description?: string;
    readonly type: string;
    /** Task name this result belongs to; set when attached to a TaskDef. */
    private taskName?: string;

    constructor(opts: ResultOptions) { /* ... */ }

    /** Internal: sets the owning task name so the path/reference expressions work. */
    _bindToTask(taskName: string): void { this.taskName = taskName; }

    /** Path inside the step container where this result should be written. */
    get path(): string { return `$(results.${this.name}.path)`; }

    /** Pipeline-level reference: `$(tasks.<task>.results.<name>)`. */
    toString(): string {
      if (!this.taskName) throw new Error(`Result '${this.name}' not bound to a task`);
      return `$(tasks.${this.taskName}.results.${this.name})`;
    }

    toSpec(): Record<string, unknown> { /* { name, type, description? } */ }
  }
  ```
- File: `src/index.ts` — export `Result` and `ResultOptions`.
- New test file: `src/lib/core/result.test.ts` — verify `path`, `toString` after
  bind, `toSpec` output.

## Acceptance
- `flox activate -- npm test` — new result.test.ts passes.
- `flox activate -- npm run build` — clean compile.

## Hints
- Mirror `Param` exactly. Read `src/lib/core/param.ts` first.
- `toString` throwing pre-bind is a deliberate choice — it surfaces "result used
  before attaching to a task" as a clear error. Test this behavior.

## Why
The TaskLike implementation that represents a remote, hub-resolved Task.
Pipelines reference it like any other TaskDef; TektonProject knows not to synth
a Task resource for it (T1.3 already handles this).

## What to change
- New file: `src/lib/core/hub-task-ref.ts`.
  ```ts
  export interface HubTaskRefOptions {
    /** Hub catalog name (e.g. 'tekton'). */
    catalog?: string;
    /** Task name in the catalog (e.g. 'git-clone'). */
    taskName: string;
    /** Task version (e.g. '0.9'). */
    version: string;
    /** Local node name in the pipeline. Defaults to taskName. */
    name?: string;
    /** Params the user will pass to this task — must match the published Task's params. */
    params?: Param[];
    /** Workspaces the user will bind to this task — must match the published Task's workspaces. */
    workspaces?: Workspace[];
    /** Tasks that must complete before this one runs. */
    needs?: TaskLike[];
  }

  export class HubTaskRef implements TaskLike {
    readonly name: string;
    readonly params: Param[];
    readonly workspaces: Workspace[];
    readonly needs: TaskLike[];
    readonly synthesizable = false;
    private readonly catalog: string;
    private readonly taskName: string;
    private readonly version: string;

    constructor(opts: HubTaskRefOptions) { /* ... */ }

    _toPipelineTaskSpec(runAfterNames: string[], _namePrefix?: string): Record<string, unknown> {
      const spec: Record<string, unknown> = {
        name: this.name,
        taskRef: {
          resolver: 'hub',
          params: [
            { name: 'catalog', value: this.catalog },
            { name: 'name', value: this.taskName },
            { name: 'version', value: this.version },
          ],
        },
      };
      if (this.params.length > 0) {
        spec.params = this.params.map(p => ({ name: p.name, value: p.pipelineExpression ?? `$(params.${p.name})` }));
      }
      if (this.workspaces.length > 0) {
        spec.workspaces = this.workspaces.map(w => ({ name: w.name, workspace: w.name }));
      }
      if (runAfterNames.length > 0) spec.runAfter = runAfterNames;
      return spec;
    }
  }
  ```
- File: `src/index.ts` — export `HubTaskRef` and `HubTaskRefOptions`.

## Acceptance
- `flox activate -- npm run build` clean.
- `flox activate -- npm test` passes.

## Hints
- Mirror `_toPipelineTaskSpec` from `TaskDef` for shape consistency.
- `catalog` defaults to `'tekton'` — that's the most common case.
- Do not include `kind: Task` when using a resolver — Tekton rejects it.

## Depends on
- T1.1 (TaskLike interface).
- T1.3 (TektonProject already skips synth for these).

Once both providers publish from their own repos:
- delete packages/tektonic-cache-gcs and packages/tektonic-reporter-github; decide whether to flatten packages/tektonic to the repo root (one package no longer needs npm workspaces or tsc -b);
- examples/self-ci.ts imports the providers from npm instead of ../packages/*/dist — note the release-ordering consequence: a core major bump cannot be used by core's own self-CI until the providers publish a release accepting it;
- scripts/check-provider-imports.mjs becomes unnecessary (physical separation enforces it); remove it and the lint:imports/typecheck scripts, or keep an equivalent check in the provider repos;
- renovate.json fileFilters and postUpgradeTasks paths; publish.yml's workspace loop (handed off as a patch);
- CHANGELOG: note that provider changes are now logged in their own repos;
- docs (status-reporters.md, cache-backends.md, job-libraries.md, architecture.md, README, CONTRIBUTING): link the provider repos as reference implementations of the extension points.

## Why
Define the contract before refactoring. This shapes the surface area future
providers must implement.

