## Why
Introduce a wrapper type for per-pipeline task overrides — starting with `when`,
but designed to extend to `retries`, `timeout`, etc. This is the design vehicle
for option 2 in the parent epic.

## What to change
- New file: `src/lib/core/pipeline-task.ts`.
  ```ts
  export interface WhenExpression {
    input: string;          // e.g. "$(params.event-type)"
    operator: 'in' | 'notin';
    values: string[];
  }

  export interface PipelineTaskOverrides {
    when?: WhenExpression[];
  }

  export interface PipelineTaskNode extends TaskLike {
    readonly _overrides: PipelineTaskOverrides;
  }

  /** Wraps a TaskLike with per-pipeline-edge overrides. */
  export function gated(task: TaskLike, overrides: PipelineTaskOverrides): PipelineTaskNode {
    // Returns an object that delegates to `task` for everything except
    // `_toPipelineTaskSpec`, which merges `when` into the emitted spec.
    return new Proxy(task as PipelineTaskNode, {
      get(target, prop) {
        if (prop === '_overrides') return overrides;
        if (prop === '_toPipelineTaskSpec') {
          return (runAfter: string[], prefix?: string) => {
            const base = task._toPipelineTaskSpec(runAfter, prefix);
            if (overrides.when?.length) base.when = overrides.when;
            return base;
          };
        }
        return Reflect.get(target, prop);
      },
    });
  }
  ```
- File: `src/index.ts` — export `gated`, `WhenExpression`, `PipelineTaskOverrides`.

## Acceptance
- `flox activate -- npm run build` clean.
- `flox activate -- npm test` — existing tests untouched.

## Hints
- Using a Proxy avoids the need to define a wrapper class with delegate methods
  for every TaskLike field. Tradeoff: slightly less greppable. If you prefer a
  plain class, that is fine — the interface is what matters.

## Depends on
- T1.1 (TaskLike).
